### 2.2 Proto Contract Definition (`proto/account_service.proto`)
Protobuf v3 `optional` keyword is used to differentiate between an explicitly set status and an omitted field (`null`/no-op).

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package account.v1;

option go_package = "github.com/org/account/v1;accountv1";

enum AccountStatus {
  ACCOUNT_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
  ACCOUNT_STATUS_ACTIVE = 1;
  ACCOUNT_STATUS_INACTIVE = 2;
}

message UpdateAccountRequest {
  string account_id = 1;
  optional AccountStatus status = 2; // Supports presence tracking (null vs ACTIVE vs INACTIVE)
  optional string display_name = 3;
}

message UpdateAccountResponse {
  string account_id = 1;
  AccountStatus status = 2;
  string display_name = 3;
  int64 updated_at_unix_ms = 4;
}

service AccountService {
  rpc UpdateAccount (UpdateAccountRequest) returns (UpdateAccountResponse);
}
```

### 2.3 Field Mapping Strategy
| Legacy JSON Payload | Proto Request (`UpdateAccountRequest`) | Domain Model Action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `{"status": "ACTIVE"}` | `status = ACCOUNT_STATUS_ACTIVE` | Set `status = Status.ACTIVE` |
| `{"status": "INACTIVE"}` | `status = ACCOUNT_STATUS_INACTIVE` | Set `status = Status.INACTIVE` |
| `{}` or `{"status": null}` | `status = null` (`!has_status()`) | Do not mutate `status` (partial patch) |
| `{"status": "INVALID"}` | Validation Error (`InvalidArgument`) | Abort with gRPC status `INVALID_ARGUMENT` |

